{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi","id":1232071,"title":"how do the incarna fare in a fight with a primordial/yozi?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-03T02:28:25-07:00","id":1232071,"title":"how do the incarna fare in a fight with a primordial/yozi?","content":"not counting the sun himself(with temperance on anyway) as in, has anyone tried to play test Luna versus the ED or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T04:00:00-07:00","id":1232080,"title":"","content":"Wouldnt it be a bit hard to do since Gods have built in mechanisms saying they cannot hurt a Primordial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T05:15:26-07:00","id":1232092,"title":"","content":"At least in 3E, I would argue that the enemies of the gods (and to a lesser extent the Incarnae) should avoid being quantified by the game's system. Lesser representations and souls aside, the real answer to the question about how to fight them should be &quot;through story.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T05:22:10-07:00","id":1232094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232080#post1232080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldnt it be a bit hard to do since Gods have built in mechanisms saying they cannot hurt a Primordial?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since that's not a mechanical thing, it doesn't seem like a meaningful impediment to mark's question.<br /> <br /> I've never actually done anything like run such a test myself, but offhand I would say that the kinds of powers that Luna had in Glories would make her at least as threatening to a Primordial as the Sun is. I can't quite remember all of them, but... didn't she have something to immunise herself against sources of damage?<br /> <br /> I think that the Maidens might need to be in concert to do so, and only if it turns out that samsara foretells the defeat of the Primordials.","signature":"<hr class=\"