b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's an implicit &quot;assuming the geass against harming the primordails was somehow disabled...&quot; in the OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering past threads, I wouldn't be so quick to assume that. Quite a few threads of this type get started with the OP just plain not being aware of something pretty central to the whole discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T10:38:26-07:00","id":1232168,"title":"","content":"Haven't tested, but I feel worth noting for the folks saying that &quot;3e's fluff isn't there/they aren't statted/etc&quot;, the OP is clearly working with 2e Paradigms (hence UCS having a tempermance or Valor effect).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T12:29:12-07:00","id":1232206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232161#post1232161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering past threads, I wouldn't be so quick to assume that. Quite a few threads of this type get started with the OP just plain not being aware of something pretty central to the whole discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, my bad, i forgot to write &quot;assume the geas is disabled&quot; also assume that the duel happens under &quot;fair&quot;(i.e if a primordial/incarna is good in straight white room fights but his/her opponent is good in more subtle &quot;dark room &quot; ways then the &quot;arena&quot; should be neutral. also i am assuming a 2e or 2.5e edition given that 3.e has no statted incarna/yozis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T13:00:39-07:00","id":1232210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232206#post1232206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah, my bad, i forgot to write &quot;assume the geas is disabled&quot; also assume that the duel happens under &quot;fair&quot;(i.e if a primordial/incarna is good in straight white room fights but his/her opponent is good in more subtle &quot;dark room &quot; ways then the &quot;arena&quot; should be neutral. also i am assuming a 2e or 2.5e edition given that 3.e has no statted incarna/yozis</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno\u2026 I feel as though both Luna and any given Yozi that she might theoretically be fighting are capable of warping the nature of the playing field, or dragging an opponent into an entirely new one, in order to make the conditions more favourable. It's hard to limit a Yozi to a white room when a number of those beings consist of sizable landscapes.<br /> <br /> Even Second Edition never got around to elaborating on how things like a Yozis's awareness interact with the scope of their own bodies and the scale at which other beings exist, so some of that needs to be adjudicated. Take Cecylene, for instance; being &quot;in&quot; a white room is kind of irrelevant considering how she stretches to infinity, and assuming that she's not omniscient as regards her own form, Luna can acquire a number of environmental advantages as regards going around as any kind of desert creature, desert creature native to Cecylene, or associated First Circle Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T13:15:07-07:00","id":1232213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232210#post1232210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno\u2026 I feel as though both Luna and any given Yozi that she might theoretically be fighting are capable of warping the nature of the playing field, or dragging an opponent into an entirely new one, in order to make the conditions more favourable. It's hard to limit a Yozi to a white room when a number of those beings consist of sizable landscapes.<br /> <br /> Even Second Edition never got around to elaborating on how things like a Yozis's awareness interact with the scope of their own bodies and the scale at which other beings exist, so some of that needs to be adjudicated. Take Cecylene, for instance; being &quot;in&quot; a white room is kind of irrelevant considering how she stretches to infinity, and assuming that she's not omniscient as regards her own form, Luna can acquire a number of environmental advantages as regards going around as any kind of desert creature, desert creature native to Cecylene, or associated First Circle Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as Primordial awareness goes in 2e it was stated that they were capable of knowing everything going on inside of their own body.* It was mentioned that if Malfeas wanted to he could know every detail of all things going on inside of the demon city since he is the demon city. So a &quot;white room&quot; fight against a primordial with a world body like Malfeas, Cecylene, Kimberry, etc would likely end up defaulting to a fight inside the Primordial's world body if only because I can't imagine any of them not wanting to be able to remind their enemy of just how out of their depth they are. <br /> <br /> *They're just solipistic and concerned with matters so far above everything else that they aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T14:04:23-07:00","id":1232221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232213#post1232213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as Primordial awareness goes in 2e it was stated that they were capable of knowing everything going on inside of their own body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T14:34:04-07:00","id":1232229,"title":"","content":"It's really hard to say because while there was an insistence was that he represented the lower end of a Primordial's power, The Ebon Dragon was impressively pathetic and when Bastet ran a fight between him and the Scarlet Empress he was losing against her pretty badly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T14:40:42-07:00","id":1232231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232221#post1232221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 78 Compass of Celestial Directions: Malfeas states Malfeas can be as aware as he bloody well wants to be and it would be within his power to know everything going on in the Demon City.* Page 51 also notes that the Yozi are capable of knowing anything they want to know, but usually aren't interested in knowing about insects entering their world. <br /> <br /> <br /> *Granted this is also an ST advice section, so it is pointing out that such a level of awareness and activity would probably be undesired for most games. Though I can see it being useful if one wants to run a game of Paranoia in Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T14:43:11-07:00","id":1232232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232229#post1232229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really hard to say because while there was an insistence was that he represented the lower end of a Primordial's power, The Ebon Dragon was impressively pathetic and when Bastet ran a fight between him and the Scarlet Empress he was losing against her pretty badly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the one time my circle fought him in 2e, my character was the only one able to hit him consistently, but he punched off half his health bar in a single turn with his Combo, leading to him fleeing away.<br /> <br /> If anyone here is disappointed by how anti-climactic that sounds, yeah, you're not the only one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-04-2018, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T14:55:37-07:00","id":1232235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232231#post1232231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Granted this is also an ST advice section, so it is pointing out that such a level of awareness and activity would probably be undesired for most games.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is what I've talked about before, with the idea of writing things in terms of thinking about the minutia of metaphysics and deriving &quot;logical&quot; consequences to them, as prioritized over significance or utility in gameplay, ala &quot;Abyssals and Alchemicals cannot become akuma, because something something incompatible Primordial Essence&quot;.<br /> <br /> I ask you, what is the point? What is the point of saying that Malfeas has that level of awareness, at the same time as admitting that it's a bad thing for functional games? For Gawd's sake.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if Cecylene or Malfeas or whomever has such awareness, then it needs to go into what powers Luna might have to assist in stealth or being unrecognised while in any of the infinite possible forms that she can take, as she goes around doing something clandestine and dangerous. It still leaves a scenario more complicated than the ultimate shapeshifting trickster goddess and the infinite desert standing at opposite ends of a white room, and slugging it out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T15:17:48-07:00","id":1232238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232235#post1232235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It still leaves a scenario <b>more complicated</b> than the ultimate shapeshifting trickster goddess and the infinite desert standing at opposite ends of a white room, and slugging it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>And more compelling.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T15:24:26-07:00","id":1232240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232231#post1232231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I can see it being useful if one wants to run a game of Paranoia in Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well look at this friend with the fantastic ideas.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12603-molotove","name":"Molotove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T07:06:40-07:00","id":1232361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232213#post1232213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as Primordial awareness goes in 2e it was stated that they were capable of knowing everything going on inside of their own body.* It was mentioned that if Malfeas wanted to he could know every detail of all things going on inside of the demon city since he is the demon city. So a &quot;white room&quot; fight against a primordial with a world body like Malfeas, Cecylene, Kimberry, etc would likely end up defaulting to a fight inside the Primordial's world body if only because I can't imagine any of them not wanting to be able to remind their enemy of just how out of their depth they are.<br /> <br /> *They're just solipistic and concerned with matters so far above everything else that they aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i would argue that fighting a primordial solely within his world-body probably counts as advantageous to the primordial. Plus a released Malfeas(capable of seeking such a duel to begin with) would no longer be inside out . as is the case with most other primordials(even if they can still have rather huge joutens)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T07:28:26-07:00","id":1232364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232361#post1232361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus a released Malfeas would no longer be inside out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you cite your sources on this one? If you mutilate a guy and toss his ass in jail, letting him out afterward doesn't un-mutilate him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T08:04:32-07:00","id":1232379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232364#post1232364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you cite your sources on this one? If you mutilate a guy and toss his ass in jail, letting him out afterward doesn't un-mutilate him.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> except malfeas isn't &quot;in jail&quot; he is the jail. this is what &quot;inside out&quot; means in this context . His inner worlds(such as the ones that devil-tigers infernals can develop and that all primordials have ) are &quot;outer&quot; now. For instance IIRC compass of celestial directions: Malfeas(either that or the book about demons) says that 100 years after his imprisonment malfeas tried to cast a ritual to undo his inversion and become free","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T08:08:34-07:00","id":1232383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232229#post1232229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really hard to say because while there was an insistence was that he represented the lower end of a Primordial's power, The Ebon Dragon was impressively pathetic and when Bastet ran a fight between him and the Scarlet Empress he was losing against her pretty badly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Really? That's interesting. Was it because he couldn't perfect Holy effects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T12:38:28-07:00","id":1232469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232383#post1232383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? That's interesting. Was it because he couldn't perfect Holy effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly. Dragon Vortex from an essence 8 Dragon-Blooded is Holy and deals aggravated damage to Creatures of Darkness so he needed to roll 24 successes to avoid damage. The -8 environmental penalty severely limited his options because he's cartoonishly weak for something 50 miles long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T08:15:53-07:00","id":1232628,"title":"","content":"Ebon Dragon is a very elaborate joke on Neph's behalf. He is a powergamer who tried to rules-lawyer himself an ever-applicable perfect defense by making himself vulnerable only to a being which categorically cannot hurt him (originally only the TUCS had access to Holy effects, but couldn't touch TED due to the Primordial Geas) but got hoisted by his own petard when the Exalted came into being with the ability to channel some Holy for themselves, and now he's got a strong contender for the most debilitating Flaw of Invulnerability in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T09:35:51-07:00","id":1232641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232379#post1232379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> except malfeas isn't &quot;in jail&quot; he is the jail. this is what &quot;inside out&quot; means in this context . His inner worlds(such as the ones that devil-tigers infernals can develop and that all primordials have ) are &quot;outer&quot; now. For instance IIRC compass of celestial directions: Malfeas(either that or the book about demons) says that 100 years after his imprisonment malfeas tried to cast a ritual to undo his inversion and become free</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't that a plan to essentially change the definition of the prison though? Currently Malfeas is inverted and all the yozis are imprisoned inside him, but if he changes which side 'inside' is then everybody is essentially free without breaking any surrender oaths.<br /> <br /> Similar to how the reclamation in 2E was predicated on the idea that turning everything into the same as Malfeas means the yozi would be free to wander around again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T10:41:19-07:00","id":1232654,"title":"","content":"In the fiction where Theion (now Malfeas) created the Unconquered Sun, it stated that Theion was impressed because TUCS was greater then his creator. If Sol Invictis was greater then Theion, he's most assuredly stronger then Malfeas, who like the other Yozi are less then they once were. I would assess that Luna would be fairly close to TUCS in power, with the Maidens only bit behind her. So in this theoretical brawl between the Incarnae and the Yozi, I feel like the Yozi would really dislike the results of such an engagement.<br /> <br /> Having said that, I don't see such a battle as feasible at all. The geas that prevents the gods from harming the Primordials/Yozi can't be removed. It was built into then. If it could be removed, they would have done it long ago. Even after the Yozi were imprisoned, all the Exalts combined (Solars with 3rd Circle Sorcery, the Lunars and Sidereals, and close to a million Dragonbloods) still didn't remove the geas. Even with the Yozi imprisoned, there are a lot of good reasons to remove the geas, but they still didn't. So I don't see the gods ever being able to harm a Yozi, and considering their power, I don't see the Yozi directly attacking them unless their lives depended on it (which their lives will never depend on it as the Gods can't harm them). It's a circle of reasoning that means they'll never engage each other directly. This is my own interpretation though, so perhaps others have a different viewpoint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 07-05-2018, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T11:05:29-07:00","id":1232660,"title":"","content":"The 'geas' was built into 2e Infernal charms. Unquestionable Yozi Authority, has the ability to make an Infernal immune to demons and gods. If you have Essence 10 it would apply to all demons and gods. At one point or another Neph explicitly stated that this charm, and others like it that all Primordials have, was the mechanism that prevented the Gods from harming the Primordials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T11:54:52-07:00","id":1232668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232628#post1232628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ebon Dragon is a very elaborate joke on Neph's behalf. He is a powergamer who tried to rules-lawyer himself an ever-applicable perfect defense by making himself vulnerable only to a being which categorically cannot hurt him (originally only the TUCS had access to Holy effects, but couldn't touch TED due to the Primordial Geas) but got hoisted by his own petard when the Exalted came into being with the ability to channel some Holy for themselves, and now he's got a strong contender for the most debilitating Flaw of Invulnerability in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's got another one that a lot of people don't immediately notice.<br /> His perfect has the Shaping keyword so something that defends against it within an Area of Effect also shuts down his ability to defend himself. So something like the Abyssal charm Dream Slaying Defence arguably shut down half of the Infernal Perfect Defences (Sand Through Fingers Defence and Counter-Conceptual Interposition are also Shaping) through mere proximity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232660#post1232660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 'geas' was built into 2e Infernal charms. Unquestionable Yozi Authority, has the ability to make an Infernal immune to demons and gods. If you have Essence 10 it would apply to all demons and gods. At one point or another Neph explicitly stated that this charm, and others like it that all Primordials have, was the mechanism that prevented the Gods from harming the Primordials.</div> </div> </div> </div> It should be noted it prevents the gods from <i>directly</i> harming them. But specifically points out edge cases where harm can be done like attacking a mountain to cause a landslide.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T11:59:13-07:00","id":1232669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232668#post1232668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's got another one that a lot of people don't immediately notice.<br /> His perfect has the Shaping keyword so something that defends against it within an Area of Effect also shuts down his ability to defend himself. So something like the Abyssal charm Dream Slaying Defence arguably shut down half of the Infernal Perfect Defences (Sand Through Fingers Defence and Counter-Conceptual Interposition are also Shaping) through mere proximity.<br /> <br /> It should be noted it prevents the gods from <i>directly</i> harming them. But specifically points out edge cases where harm can be done like attacking a mountain to cause a landslide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lucky them that pretty much all the geographical features of any size where they live are also Yozi then I guess :-P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T12:40:34-07:00","id":1232683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232660#post1232660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 'geas' was built into 2e Infernal charms. Unquestionable Yozi Authority, has the ability to make an Infernal immune to demons and gods. If you have Essence 10 it would apply to all demons and gods. At one point or another Neph explicitly stated that this charm, and others like it that all Primordials have, was the mechanism that prevented the Gods from harming the Primordials.</div> </div> </div> </div>the geas was later retconned. it no longer applies to the celestial incarna(and presumably,fetich souls) Instead the geas of the incarna is a built in mechanism(or flaw)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T13:08:40-07:00","id":1232686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232683#post1232683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the geas was later retconned. it no longer applies to the celestial incarna(and presumably,fetich souls) Instead the geas of the incarna is a built in mechanism(or flaw)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Have I mentioned I hate the GotMH errata? Because I hate the GotMH errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T14:26:05-07:00","id":1232703,"title":"","content":"But yes a big part of the Ebon Dragon's weakness comes from the overall design direction of 2nd edition Infernals making him to all intents and purposes a cripplingly overspecialised elder exalt.<br /> <br /> While he is the weakest to a major extent this does inform what the other Yozis will look like. Anyone who thinks Malfeas is going to have strength, soak and health levels in the trillions simply wasn't paying attention to the 2e paradigm and writer statements that an essence 10 Solar becoming a Primordial is moving sideways not upwards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T17:50:19-07:00","id":1232760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232703#post1232703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yes a big part of the Ebon Dragon's weakness comes from the overall design direction of 2nd edition Infernals making him to all intents and purposes a cripplingly overspecialised elder exalt.<br /> <br /> While he is the weakest to a major extent this does inform what the other Yozis will look like. Anyone who thinks Malfeas is going to have strength, soak and health levels in the trillions simply wasn't paying attention to the 2e paradigm and writer statements that an essence 10 Solar becoming a Primordial is moving sideways not upwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>He would most likely have that though. Malfeas is literally the size of either the blessed isle or creation. He has multiple layers within himself. You'd have to find something specific to target. Moreover, attacking him inside himself will never work as he can never not be the demon city. That is too say, unlike the ebon dragon, he always qualifies for his perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T18:41:23-07:00","id":1232766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232760#post1232760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He would most likely have that though.</div> </div> </div> </div>If he was stated by someone who wanted to masturbate over Malfeas at the expense of how Infernal charms are supposed to work and the outcome of the Primordial War. Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T19:47:16-07:00","id":1232781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232766#post1232766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he was stated by someone who wanted to masturbate over Malfeas at the expense of how Infernal charms are supposed to work and the outcome of the Primordial War. Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to him being stated the way he should be. As a structure that's as big as a world. Specific areas would probably need to be targeted as weak points, but you'd still have to find them. Currently, in 2e those charms canonically allow malfeas to perfectly everything so long as he has motes. He and adjoran got perfects that will never not work on them. He is always in a city and she is always running. Moreover, Infernal charms were changed in 3e to no longer be the charmset of the primordial's for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T20:06:00-07:00","id":1232785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232781#post1232781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referring to him being stated the way he should be. As a structure that's as big as a world. Specific areas would probably need to be targeted as weak points, but you'd still have to find them. Currently, in 2e those charms canonically allow malfeas to perfectly everything so long as he has motes. He and adjoran got perfects that will never not work on them. He is always in a city and she is always running. Moreover, Infernal charms were changed in 3e to no longer be the charmset of the primordial's for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really a good argument tactic to use two different editions as two different points.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T20:33:35-07:00","id":1232788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232785#post1232785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really a good argument tactic to use two different editions as two different points.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue stems from the problems that arises in my points. We only have the charms for the beings in question in 2e. However, the issue with tying them to infernals is that the current canon (3e) is moving away from them is a good reason.<br /> <br /> In 2e, some primordials were broken and other primordials were underpowered. However, if we use 2e, malfeas would be one of the more impossible yozi to deal with. You can't really remove malfeas from himself so there's no way to stop him from perfecting all attacks by any of the incarnae even if they could attack him. Adjoran would be the same because they don't have the tools to stop her from running. At the same time, both of them have charms to cause the unconquered sun and luna to waste enough resources or cause virtue conflicts to get through their defenses. The problem with 2e is that as soon as one of them gets through the perfect, they automatically win. There is no way for either side to successfully deal with what's essentially for all purposes infinite damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T07:13:23-07:00","id":1232850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232781#post1232781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referring to him being stated the way he should be. As a structure that's as big as a world. Specific areas would probably need to be targeted as weak points, but you'd still have to find them. Currently, in 2e those charms canonically allow malfeas to perfectly everything so long as he has motes. He and adjoran got perfects that will never not work on them. He is always in a city and she is always running. Moreover, Infernal charms were changed in 3e to no longer be the charmset of the primordial's for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> do keep in a mind that primordials also have a greater imperfection.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232628#post1232628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ebon Dragon is a very elaborate joke on Neph's behalf. He is a powergamer who tried to rules-lawyer himself an ever-applicable perfect defense by making himself vulnerable only to a being which categorically cannot hurt him (originally only the TUCS had access to Holy effects, but couldn't touch TED due to the Primordial Geas) but got hoisted by his own petard when the Exalted came into being with the ability to channel some Holy for themselves, and now he's got a strong contender for the most debilitating Flaw of Invulnerability in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>most likely the dragon's shadow had a different imperfection. after all he existed before the sun did. Not sure whether the creation of the sun immediately changed it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232686#post1232686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Have I mentioned I hate the GotMH errata? Because I hate the GotMH errata.</div> </div> </div> </div> just curious, any particular reason for this? why is it a good idea for pcs to have the geas against the incarna?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> going back to Incarna vs Primordials does anyone know if any books talk about this possibility?(such as if Malfeas lifts his geas temporarily which he can still do)<br /> i know that by canon a primordial has more raw power than an incarna (even the sun is technically weaker but also super efficient but they are also less versatile.)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 07-06-2018, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T08:15:45-07:00","id":1232862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232668#post1232668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be noted it prevents the gods from <i>directly</i> harming them. But specifically points out edge cases where harm can be done like attacking a mountain to cause a landslide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that is how the gods were able to make the Exalted to fight/kill the primordials, by exploiting that edge case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T10:00:04-07:00","id":1232875,"title":"","content":"You don't build &quot;don't attack me&quot; clauses in to your creations if they're not a legitimate threat.<br /> <br /> The incarnae as a whole would curbstomp any individual Primordial. One on one, any of the incarnae is a serious threat. Luna is perhaps the deadliest threat- she was specifically designed as an anti-primordial weapon, after all. If she can't make you fall in love with her or take your jouten body in a straight up fight (and she might! She's good at both of those things!), she's very very good at stealthily hunting down your souls one by one and devouring them, and unlike the sun she's perfectly willing to cheat and use dishonorable tactics to take you down.<br /> <br /> ... don't mess with Luna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T10:28:35-07:00","id":1232877,"title":"","content":"The only direct statement that I can recall about this is a 2e one stating, if I recall correctly, that the UCS could potentially (as in, he has a chance, not that he definitely would) beat any Primordial one-on-one if he weren't bound by the Geas. Of course, that may or may not still be canon. Either way I'm not sure it's a useful question to focus on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T14:48:36-07:00","id":1232933,"title":"","content":"Being invulnerable and being able to do infinite damage definitely gives him a shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T16:23:24-07:00","id":1232950,"title":"","content":"Some of it comes down to how their perfect defenses with their &quot;greater flaws&quot; operate (i.e. Malfeas always counts as a city for the purpose of his lesser flaw of invulnerability, so he has a greater one that kicks in with his Essence 10 charms like the Ebon Dragon does).<br /> <br /> Also the Unconquered Sun depends on which ruleset you're using. In the printed Glories rules, he's a one hit wonder if he's suppressing Temperance. In the errata, he's much tougher, but also loses everything that made his original ruleset cool - essentially becoming an extended video game boss fighting where you're knocking off arms all day. I came up with alternate errata that gives him a Perfect Parry with the Dayspear (that also lets him make an attack with it) that costs essence and willpower, provided he's upholding his Valor and at least Compassion or Conviction (so his Valor must be being upheld in service to a greater purpose for it to work). That way he has a dangerous combat mode for when he's suppressing Temperance, but it's still directly tied to his Virtues, and you can still disarm him by catching him in Virtue contradictions as per the original rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T18:34:57-07:00","id":1232971,"title":"","content":"You know, nobody ever seemed to talk about it, but I'm pretty sure that the errata changed the Sun's defence so that he still has a perfect when Temperance is suppressed, it just cost him motes and Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T18:43:26-07:00","id":1232974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232875#post1232875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't build &quot;don't attack me&quot; clauses in to your creations if they're not a legitimate threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually had this elaborate thought on combat doctrines for Primordials and how that may have shaped the War of the Gods that maybe I'll talk about at some point if I ever get my act back together and feel as though anybody is interested, but the basic foundational premise of it is &quot;the Primordials were immensely powerful, but kind of cowardly (or at least impatient)&quot;.<br /> <br /> An idea that their first priority is not remotely liking to do anything with any entity that has the slightest chance of harming them, and that their second is that is anything is capable of surviving a Primordial breathing on it, glancing at it, or tossing a mountain in its direction, then it's too much effort for them to deal with directly (or even indirectly).<br /> <br /> So they geased the gods and other supernatural beings out of fear, and had the Unconquered Sun to deal with basically anything from the Wyld, even though the majority of these things probably don't have defences against uncountable levels of damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T03:20:59-07:00","id":1233161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232877#post1232877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only direct statement that I can recall about this is a 2e one stating, if I recall correctly, that the UCS could potentially (as in, he has a chance, not that he definitely would) beat any Primordial one-on-one if he weren't bound by the Geas. Of course, that may or may not still be canon. Either way I'm not sure it's a useful question to focus on.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, that's from manual of exalted power:infernals,though it does say that the primordials are still stronger(in the sense of having more spiritual mojo) than he is. the implication being that they are less efficient &quot;machines&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T14:25:06-07:00","id":1233507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1232781#post1232781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referring to him being stated the way he should be. As a structure that's as big as a world. Specific areas would probably need to be targeted as weak points, but you'd still have to find them.</div> </div> </div> </div> If this is achieved through bloated numbers its a shocking failure of imagination.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently, in 2e those charms canonically allow malfeas to perfectly everything so long as he has motes. He and adjoran got perfects that will never not work on them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He is always in a city and she is always running.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is he always a city? Or is that an aspect of his imprisonment? Can he even fight as a city?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, Infernal charms were changed in 3e to no longer be the charmset of the primordial's for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>If 3e sees fit to give him a statline he will be able to loose to 5 Exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T14:31:47-07:00","id":1233511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1233507#post1233507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If 3e sees fit to give him a statline he will be able to loose to 5 Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know... that's fine for the Unconquered Sun, but I feel as though for an entire Primordial, something a bit more extreme might be necessary.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T14:38:09-07:00","id":1233514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1233511#post1233511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know... that's fine for the Unconquered Sun, but I feel as though for an <b>entire Primordial</b>, something a bit more extreme might be necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its not though. You fall into the trap of 2e Infernals by assuming the Jouten/world body is the &quot;real&quot; Primordial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T14:39:40-07:00","id":1233516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1233507#post1233507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is he always a city? Or is that an aspect of his imprisonment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, he's a city. Always. If you're talking about the him that's a building then it's always in a city, if you're talking about the brass dancer, good luck taking that <i>out</i> of the city. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1233507#post1233507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can he even fight as a city?</div> </div> </div> </div>He's able to crash several layers of himself together, crushing thousands or millions of inhabitants. He does this on a regular basis. This is referred to frequently in MoEP: Infernals. Like, a lot. I don't think it's difficult to imagine him fighting using his city jotun. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1233507#post1233507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If 3e sees fit to give him a statline he will be able to loose to 5 Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T14:49:47-07:00","id":1233518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1233516#post1233516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, he's a city. Always. If you're talking about the him that's a building then it's always in a city, if you're talking about the brass dancer, good luck taking that <i>out</i> of the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. He has always been a city, but he has also always been an inside-out prison for his brethren.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's able to crash several layers of himself together, crushing thousands or millions of inhabitants. He does this on a regular basis. This is referred to frequently in MoEP: Infernals.</div> </div> </div> </div>The extent to which this is fighting with a statblock is something I question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by this?</div> </div> </div> </div> 3e is not going to stat an enemy that is unbeatable as far as most games are concerned.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T15:13:34-07:00","id":1233524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1233514#post1233514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You fall into the trap of 2e Infernals by assuming the Jouten/world body is the &quot;real&quot; Primordial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nooooo, I'm not. My position is based on what I think would be interesting and make for a compelling image of the Primordial War, not some kind of logical extrapolation from scant information.<br /> <br /> Second Edition was the one that said that killing its human-shaped/sized body was sufficient to kill the entire thing, wasn't it?<br /> <br /> Games of Divinity described Yozis as having a true form, and I always read that as referring to their respective iconic forms, but that's probably different from the idea of one being more real than the others, to be sure.<br /> <br /> Still, if you're saying what I think you are, I personally find the idea that the key to slaying a Primordial to be confronting it in a human size to be not very interesting.<br /> <br /> Mind, my current conception of Yozis, going by Third Edition systems, is one in which a battle against one at your level is among the <i>most</i> dangerous times to do so. Malfeas' city body can only really deal in uncountable damage (the easiest for something like Heavenly Guardian Defence or Adamant Skin Technique to deal with), and has a long wind up time on throwing those mountains at you. If Malfeas comes down to your level, with power concentrated into something like high-end combat Charms and large dice pools, where Heavenly Guardian Defence will only save you if you have at least as much Initiative as the enemy's attack pool, he's tremendously dangerous.<br /> <br /> He generally won't, though, because he doesn't like the kind of exertion and concentration that it entails, and he's kind of a coward. Slaying that body wouldn't take out all of him, but it would be a deep and painful wound, and more than that it's a matter of how Primordials prefer to exist; sprawling and transcendent.<br /> <br /> Still, there were Exalted who could reminisce about the War of the Gods that would tell their younger peers that <i>nothing</i> was more deadly than a cornered Primordial (with the caveat that the war was unfortunately all about cornering Primordials, because there wasn't really any ultimate strategic goal other than killing all of them).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T15:37:59-07:00","id":1233529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1233524#post1233524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second Edition was the one that said that killing its human-shaped/sized body was sufficient to kill the entire thing, wasn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div> Probably. I also meant the entire soul hierarchy for what counts as the Primordial, thats plenty unbeatable if you have the whole thing bearing down on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T17:22:11-07:00","id":1233552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232071-how-do-the-incarna-fare-in-a-fight-with-a-primordial-yozi?p=1233507#post1233507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is he always a city? Or is that an aspect of his imprisonment? Can he even fight as a city?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes he is always a city, imprisonment just folded himself into himself. He has the ability to mash his layers together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If 3e sees fit to give him a statline he will be able to loose to 5 Exalts. </div> </div> </div> We'll never see that happen again. Honestly, for good reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}